These are the original files from Pascal 2.0 as distributed by Dragon
Data under license from Microware.

If you want to run it under real OS9 remember to change NL to CR for
the text files CMDS/PascalErrs, PascalDefs and optionally Dumpreal.

Some of these files are Pascal PCODE and hence can't be disassembled.

The native modules in cmds (Pascal, PascalN, PascalS, PascalE,
PascalT.MODL, Support, Support1 and Support2) are copied from the
Dragon 64 distribution disks; their CRCs match CRCLIST. The .asm files
beside them are disassemblies of the same modules that do not assemble
(data is decoded as code and some labels are lost), so use the modules.

Compile with "pascal <prog.pas #20K", which writes the P-code to PCODEF,
and run it with "pascaln pcodef" or "pascals pcodef". Pascal reads
Pascal_Compiler from the current data directory, so copy it there.
Support and PascalErrs go in the execution directory.
